    {"route": "/clientMaster/v1/getClientMaster", "field": "clientMaster.**", "use": "extension", "target": "Company.provider_extensions", "reason": "PEO client settings: client status code, service type, billing, invoicing, commissions, GL, workers' comp policy, self-service and onboarding controls, holidays, PEO staff ids, alternate employers, and references to the PEO's check and ACH account records: checkIssueAcct, garnCheckIssueAcct, garnEftIssueAcct and cutbackCheckAcct are documented as 'ID of the checking account'; receiptCheckAcct, directDepositAccount, manualAccount and onDemandChecksAccount are described only as accounts, and are read as the same kind of reference (inferred) because their values are 1 to 3 digits with 1 to 3 distinct values across 25 clients and directDepositAccount falls back to checkIssueAcct when blank. They describe the PEO relationship (CANONICAL_MODEL section 2).", "evidence": ["contracts/prismhr/openapi/prismhr-2025.09.openapi.json#/components/schemas/ClientMaster"]},
